[This version]

Development code for joint 4 sample (nue/nuebar appearance and numu/numubar disappearance) analysis.

+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+

Building the code:

The only external (non-VALOR) dependency is ROOT. Make sure you have a functional ROOT installation.
Then, follow the next steps:

* Build the VALOR framework code (see instructions there-in).

* Use the appropriate script from the setup directory of this package (or add one for your system).
  The setup script expects two arguments:
  - the top-level source code directory of the VALOR T2K code
  - the top-level source code directory of the VALOR framework code

* Once the environment is setup, cd to the top level directory and run the configure script with
  the appropriate options for the intended analysis. See documentation there-in.

* Type make.

Example:
 % source setup/setup_at_XYZ.sh /path/to/valor/t2kana/top/level/dir /path/to/valor/fmwk/top/level/dir
 % cd /path/to/valor/t2kana/top/level/dir (or % cd $T2KOSCANA)
 % ./configure --enable-gsl-fitter --production-mode --rhc-running
 % make

If successful, you should see the libT2KNuOsc library in the fitter directory.

+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+--+

Running the analysis:

A large number of ROOT macros and batch production files are provided for each of the numerous analysis tasks.
See the RUNNING file.

To run the macros, use `root2k' instead of `root' (root2k = root + T2K oscillation analysis library).
When running a root2k script: 
  % root2k 'macros/some_script.C("/some/path/some/file.root",some_argument,another_argument,yet_another_argument)'
make sure there are NO spaces within ''.

